</TABLE>
Add components except L-cysteine&#183;HCl&#183;H<sub>2</sub>O and FeCl<sub>2</sub>&#183;4H<sub>2</sub>O to distilled water, bring volume to 1.0 L and adjust pH to 7.0.  Distribute the medium into appropriate culture vessels (e.g., 20 ml of the medium in 120 ml serum bottles) under a H<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (4:1, v/v) gas mixture, sparge with the same gas mixture for 10 - 15 min, seal with butyl rubber stoppers and autoclave. Separately autoclave concentrated (100- or 200-fold) L-cysteine&#183;HCl&#183;H<sub>2</sub>O and FeCl<sub>2</sub>&#183;4H<sub>2</sub>O solutions under a N<sub>2</sub> gas atmosphere.  Prior to inoculation, add the sterile L-cysteine&#183;HCl&#183;H<sub>2</sub>O and FeCl<sub>2</sub>&#183;4H<sub>2</sub>O solutions.  Pressurize the inoculated vessels to 100 kPa H<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (4:1, v/v) and cultivate without shaking. <br>
<I>Poorly crystalline iron(III) oxide:</I> <br>
Dissolve 108 g FeCl<sub>3</sub> in 1.0 L distilled water.  Adjust pH to 7.0 with 10 N NaOH.  Allow the suspension to sit for 30 min, then readjust pH to 7.0. Centrifuge the suspension at 5,000 x g for 20 min and pour off supernatant. Wash the precipitate with distilled water by resuspending in distilled water followed by the centrifugation.  Repeat the washing at least 5 times, then, resuspend in 1.0 L distilled water.  Use the Fe(III) suspension as 0.67 M solution.  More precisely, check the concentration of Cl<sup>-</sup> to be less than 1 mM and determine the concentration of Fe(III) by using hydroxylamine as described by Lovley and Phillips (Appl. Environ. Microbiol. 54, 751-757, 1986).  <br>
<I>Trace mineral solution:</I> <br>
Use Trace minerals of Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=151">151</a> supplemented with 0.025 g (final) Na<sub>2</sub>MoO<sub>4</sub>&#183;2H<sub>2</sub>O, 0.024 g NiCl<sub>2</sub>&#183;6H<sub>2</sub>O and 0.025 g Na<sub>2</sub>WO<sub>4</sub>&#183;2H<sub>2</sub>O (per liter).       <br>
Comment: For strain JCM 12378, inoculate with a 10% inoculum.       <br>
